<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27806" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δμώς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωός</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαμάω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>slave taken in war,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δμώων οὕς . . ληΐσσατο δῖος
			Ὀδυσσεύς</span> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δμωή</span>)
				<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.398
			</span></i>: generally, <i>slave,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεῦ δμώς εἰς ἀνδρῶν;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					24.257
				</span></i>
			: mostly in pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κτῆσιν ἐμὴν δμῶάς τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					19.333
				</span></i>
			: dat. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δμώεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					6.71
				</span></i>
			, etc.—Once in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				578
			</span></i>; freq. in <i><span class="en">E.,
				<u>Med.</u>188</span></i> (lyr.),
			al., but not found in Prose.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
